Package: tidymapr
Title: Tidy Mapping, Spatial Analysis and Publication Cartography
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jimmy", "Moses", , "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3342-2384"))
Description: A tidyverse toolkit for making publication-quality maps and
    doing spatial analysis in R, in the style of a desktop GIS. Automatic,
    explained map design (projection, classification, colour ramps,
    legends, scale bars and north arrows); reading of GIS, CAD and remote
    sensing formats; fast C++ spatial statistics (kriging with measurement
    error, local Moran's I, Getis-Ord hotspots), terrain hydrology and
    spectral indices. Compatible with the 'GeoSpaX' desktop GIS
    (<https://geospax.in4metrix.dev>): it follows
    the same cartographic conventions and reads and writes the same formats
    through 'GDAL', and runs its recipes, so maps, data and workflows
    move between the two. For ecology, it
    maps coverage-standardised diversity surfaces with uncertainty and
    spectral diversity, and works with the companion package
    'tidydiversity'.
